MewStage vendor patch multi-host/0001 (third_party/NOTICE): one process may run several embedded MewUI hosts, on
different threads (test runners run test classes in parallel) or one after another on the same thread. Three statics
assumed one UI per process: VisualTree's and LogicalTree's traversal scratch lists (two walks on two threads
corrupted each other: ArgumentOutOfRange / NullReference inside VisualTree.Visit) and
Application.DefaultGraphicsFactory, which every embedded host overwrote, so a host's elements (which resolve the
factory through it outside Application.Run) measured text with ANOTHER host's factory and two threads shared that
factory's text engine (duplicate-key exceptions in ManagedTextEngine's font caches). The scratch lists are
[ThreadStatic]; an internal Application.ThreadGraphicsFactory (per thread) wins over the process default and the
MewStage backend binds each host's factory to its UI thread. Behaviour for a single host unchanged.

